    <version>0.77.0</version>
    <time>1789395717</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.77.0, with the License tag corrected.

Supersedes 1377707, which carried the bare upstream &quot;Apache-2.0&quot;. The tag is now
re-derived from the Rust crates actually linked into /usr/bin/nono (351 crates,
from cargo's unit graph, identical on x86_64 and aarch64): Apache-2.0 AND
BSD-3-Clause AND CDLA-Permissive-2.0 AND ISC AND MIT AND MPL-2.0 AND Unicode-3.0.
MPL-2.0 comes from colored and option-ext. The derivation is documented in a
Legal-Review-Notice above the tag. The generated shell completion subpackages
declare Apache-2.0.

Local build green on openSUSE_Tumbleweed/aarch64, rpmlint 0 errors / 0 warnings.</comment>
    <requestid>1377734</requestid>
  </revision>
